            <ArticleTitle>Treatment of silent myocardial ischemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>685-96</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Long-term studies regarding the effect of treatment on prognosis are lacking, but the adverse implications suggested for silent ischemia support aggressive management. Treatment of silent ischemic episodes is possible utilizing a large variety of agents. Optimal detection and quantitation methods are still being developed, but guidelines for treatment should be similar to those for treatment of symptomatic ischemia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
